  "34": {
    "name": "Traveling",
    "main_text": "Life is a continuum without beginning or end. It goes on and on, with no ultimate goal.\n\nThe journey, the pilgrimage itself, is what gives life its character. Reaching a goal has little to do with it. To live is to dance for the sheer pleasure of dancing, without a thought for where it might lead.\n\nEveryone tries to organise life around a set of goals. But once you have reached the last one, what then? Think about what that would mean...\n\nIf you really do fulfil your ambition, you will find yourself at a loss. One day you have come to the end of the road, and along the way you have lost everything. It is inevitable.\n\nAfter pouring everything you had into a project of your own, you stand there naked and foolish. What have you really achieved?\n\nWhat was all the effort, all the rushing, all the worry for? **What did it bring you?**",
    "commentary": "This card invites us to welcome what is new, as we might on arriving in a foreign country with different customs and unfamiliar landscapes.\n\nThis openness and willingness to accept what comes bring new friends and new experiences into our lives.\n\n----------"
  },
  "35": {
    "name": "Exhaustion",
    "main_text": "Someone who lives by the dictates of a moral conscience grows rigid. Someone who lives from inner awareness stays flexible.\n\nWhy? Because a fixed idea of how your life should develop automatically makes you harden. You must constantly maintain the armour encasing your character, for it gives you protection and security.\n\nYou cease to act naturally and rely on your armour to respond to every situation. When someone asks you a question, you have a ready-made answer.\n\nMonotony, dullness and mechanical behaviour are the hallmarks of someone who has hardened. They might make a good computer, but hardly a human being. You know in advance how they will behave. Their response is as predictable as a machine's.\n\nAn authentic person acts spontaneously. They answer a question in the light of the reality of that moment. The answer is more than a reflex, because to give it **they open their heart, make themselves vulnerable and truly listen...**",
    "commentary": "Life is a mystery to be lived, rather than a business to be managed.\n\nIt is time to put away your time card, leave the factory and venture into the unknown. **You will work so much better when you are relaxed!**\n\n----------"
  },
  "36": {
    "name": "Suppression",
    "main_text": "The Sanskrit term alaya vigyan refers to a house. Into its cellar you throw everything you would have liked to do, everything you deny yourself because of social conditioning, culture and civilisation.\n\nThe things you repress keep accumulating and influence your life in subtle ways. You cannot meet them openly and directly, since you have condemned them to the dark.\n\nYet from the depths of that darkness, these repressed forces continue to shape your behaviour. They are dangerous, and keeping such forces bottled up inside is unhealthy.\n\nThey may suddenly break loose in a violent, uncontrollable outburst, a state akin to madness.\n\nParadoxically, society tolerates madness and fails to recognise meditation. Yet **it is through meditation that we become truly sane.**",
    "commentary": "It is important now to release the tension and stress that have built up inside you.\n\nPunch a pillow, jump into the air, go outside and run in the open, yell at the sky. Let loose in whatever way frees the energy inside you and allows it to flow again.\n\nDo not wait for disaster to strike.\n\n----------"
  },
  "37": {
    "name": "Healing",
    "main_text": "Your whole being is bound up with wounds you carry wherever you go. Nobody wishes to hurt or harm you. Everyone is far too busy tending to their own wounds.\n\nWhere would anyone find the energy to concern themselves with you? Yet sometimes you feel hurt because you are ready to be hurt. You stand like someone braced for a blow.\n\nA person of the Tao cannot be hurt. Why? Simply because there is nothing left inside that can be struck. No inner wound remains to be reopened. Such a person is healthy, healed, whole.\n\nThe English word â€œwholeâ€ is beautiful. â€œHealâ€ and â€œholyâ€ share its root. The person of the Tao is whole, healthy and holy.\n\nBecome aware of your wound. Instead of twisting the knife, help the wound close. It can heal only when you reach its roots.\n\nThe less you live in your head, the sooner the wound will heal. Without the mind's interference, there are no wounds. **Do not live in your head.**",
    "commentary": "Old wounds buried deep inside you are coming to the surface, ready to heal. Under the healing influence of the King of Water, we no longer hide from ourselves or from others.\n\nWith such openness and acceptance, we can heal and help others find health and wholeness too.\n\n----------"
  },
  "38": {
    "name": "Receptivity",
    "main_text": "Listening is one of the essential secrets of entering the temple of the divine. Listening is passive. It means forgetting yourself completely. That is true listening.\n\nWhen you listen closely to someone, your â€œIâ€ falls away. Unless you can step back from yourself, you cannot really listen. When you are too absorbed in yourself, you merely give the impression of listening.\n\nYou nod, you say â€œyesâ€ or â€œnoâ€ here and there, yet the other person hardly matters to you. Someone who truly listens becomes a channel.\n\nPassive and receptive like a womb, the listener becomes feminine. To reach this state, you must be feminine. You cannot reach God in the manner of an invader or a conqueror.\n\nYou will find God, or rather God will come to you, when your attitude is receptive and feminine.",
    "commentary": "The Queen of Water ushers in a time without boundaries, a time of gratitude for everything life brings, free of expectations or demands.\n\nValues such as duty, merit and reward lose their importance. Qualities like sensitivity, intuition and compassion begin to shine, sweeping away the obstacles that have kept us apart from one another and from the whole.\n\n----------"
  },
  "39": {
    "name": "Trust",
    "main_text": "Do not waste your life seeking what will be taken away from you anyway.\n\nTrust life. This is the only way to relinquish what you know and stop heeding your intellect. Out of trust, something immense will be born.\n\nThe life that until now seemed so ordinary will overflow with divine energy. When your heart is innocent and the walls around it fall, you come into contact with the infinite.\n\nYou can no longer be disappointed. Nothing remains that anyone could take away from you. What you can lose is hardly worth clinging to.\n\nAnd can you really fear losing what cannot be lost? **It is impossible to lose your true inner treasure.**",
    "commentary": "When you have the trust to take a quantum leap, preparations, plans and schedules become unnecessary.\n\nThere is no saying, â€œRight, I know exactly what I am going to do. I will pack my suitcase, buckle it up and take it along.â€ You simply leap. Just like that. Without a thought for what comes next.\n\nAll that matters is the leap itself, and the ecstasy of free fall.\n\n----------"
  },
  "40": {
    "name": "Understanding",
    "main_text": "You are no longer a prisoner. You are outside the cage. You can spread your wings, and the whole sky is yours.\n\nThe sun, the moon and every star belong to you. You can disappear into the blue beyond...\n\nStop clinging to the bars of the cage. Come outside. The endless sky is waiting. Spread your wings and fly towards the sun like an eagle.\n\nIn your inner sky, in the universe of your consciousness, freedom is the highest good. Everything else comes second, even bliss and ecstasy.\n\nThere are countless flowers, but only in a climate of freedom do they bloom.",
    "commentary": "It is natural to feel a little afraid at the first dawning of a new understanding, the realisation that the cage has always been open and the sky has long been waiting for us.\n\nYet do not let that fear take hold, or it will keep you from the great adventure before you.\n\nSurrender to the gentleness and grace of this moment. Feel the flutter of wings inside you. **Take flight and be free.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "41": {
    "name": "Going With the Flow",
    "main_text": "When I say, â€œBecome water,â€ I mean become running water. Be like water in motion. Follow the current, keep moving, never grow stagnant.\n\nThe way of the Tao is fluid. Like water, it flows of its own accord. There is beauty in the course water takes. It always seeks the depths. It knows neither ambition nor the urge to come first.\n\nWater follows its course, happy to be last. Remember the words of Jesus, â€œThe last shall be first in the kingdom of heaven.â€ Without quite naming it, he describes the flowing way of the Tao.\n\nYou too can be last, setting ambition aside. If you are always trying to stand out by being the best, you are swimming against the current.\n\nWater flows downhill. It descends to the source in the depths, seeking to be nobody at all. It makes no claim to being unique, exceptional or extraordinary. **It has no ego to maintain.**",
    "commentary": "Drawing this card suggests that you are now able to let the current carry you, trusting life to take you in the direction it has in mind for you.\n\nGive yourself over to that feeling of trust and ease. It will grow steadily within you. **Everything is unfolding just as it should.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "42": {
    "name": "Friendliness",
    "main_text": "Meditate first. Once you are at peace, love will come naturally.\n\nIt will be just as beautiful, just as wonderful, to be alone as to be in the company of others. Everything is simple. You are free from dependence on others, and they are free from dependence on you.\n\nYou will live in an atmosphere of friendship and affection, where a genuine bond exists without attachment. You can form a relationship with someone without having to marry.\n\nMarriages often rest on fear. Genuine relationships have their roots in love. They last as lYªçŠx-®éÜj×¢ëiºÚ+Š§j[h‘éÜ¢éíóM4N‹Z–‹­¦ëeŠw¬Õ½¹œ…ÌÑ¡•É”¥Ì‰•…ÕÑä…¹Í½µ•Ñ¡¥¹œÑ¼Í¡…É”¹q¹q¹]¡•¸Ñİ¼Á…Ñ¡Ì‘¥Ù•É”°Ñ¡”Ñ¥µ”¡…Ì½µ”Ñ¼Á…ÉĞ¸Q¡”±½Ù•ÉÌÍ…ä½½‘‰å”¥¸É…Ñ¥ÑÕ‘”°•… Ñ¡…¹­¥¹œÑ¡”½Ñ¡•È™½ÈÁ±…å¥¹œ…¸¥µÁ½ÉÑ…¹ĞÁ…ÉĞ¥¸Ñ¡•¥È±¥™”°™½ÈÍ¡…É¥¹œÍ¼µÕ ©½ä…¹Á±•…ÍÕÉ”…¹Í¼µ…¹ä‰•…ÕÑ¥™Õ°µ½µ•¹ÑÌ¹q¹q¹]¡•¸Á•½Á±”¡…Ù”ÑÉÕ±ä±½Ù••… ½Ñ¡•È°Ñ¡•äÁ…ÉĞİ¥Ñ¡½ÕĞ¡•…ÉÑ‰É•…¬½ÈÍÕ™™•É¥¹œ¸ˆ°(€€€€‰½µµ•¹Ñ…Éäˆè€‰¹•ÜÅÕ…±¥Ñä½˜™É¥•¹‘Í¡¥À¥Ì•¹Ñ•É¥¹œå½ÕÈ±¥™”…¹å½ÕÈÉ•±…Ñ¥½¹Í¡¥ÁÌ¸e½Ôµ…ä¹½Ñ¥”Ñ¡…Ğµ•±½‘É…µ„…¹É½µ…¹Ñ¥Œ•¹Ñ…¹±•µ•¹ÑÌ¹¼±½¹•È¡½±µÕ ¥¹Ñ•É•ÍĞ™½Èå½Ô¹q¹q¹Q¡•É”¥Ì¹¼±½ÍÌ¥¸Ñ¡¥ÌÁ…ÍÍ…”¸%Ğ¥Ì„¹•ÜÁ¡…Í”°Ñ¡”…ÉÉ¥Ù…°½˜„¡¥¡•ÈÅÕ…±¥Ñä½˜±½Ù”°‰½É¸½˜å½ÕÈ½İ¸¥¹¹•È™Õ±±¹•ÍÌ¹q¹q¹!•É”½µ•Ì€¨©Õ¹½¹‘¥Ñ¥½¹…°±½Ù”°İ¡¥ •áÁ•ÑÌ¹½Ñ¡¥¹œ…¹…Í­Ì™½È¹½Ñ¡¥¹œ¸¨©q¹q¸´´´´´´´´´´ˆ(€ô°(€€ˆĞÌˆèì(€€€€‰¹…µ”ˆè€‰•±•‰É…Ñ¥½¸ˆ°(€€€€‰µ…¥¹}Ñ•áĞˆè€‰1¥™”¥Ì„µ½µ•¹ĞÑ¼•±•‰É…Ñ”…¹Í…Ù½ÕÈ¸5…­”±¥™”„•±•‰É…Ñ¥½¸°„©½ä°…¹å½Ôİ¥±°•¹Ñ•ÈÑ¡”Ñ•µÁ±”¹q¹q¹Q¡”Ñ•µÁ±”¡…Ì¹•Ù•È‰••¸„Á±…”™½ÈÍÁ½¥±ÍÁ½ÉÑÌ¸1½½¬…Ğİ¡…Ğ•á¥ÍÑÌ…É½Õ¹å½Ô¹q¹q¹!…Ù”å½Ô•Ù•ÈÍ••¸Í…‘¹•ÍÌ¥¸¹…ÑÕÉ”üÑÉ•”¥¸„‘•ÁÉ•ÍÍ¥½¸ü‰¥É™É•ÑÑ¥¹œü¹•ÕÉ½Ñ¥Œİ¥±…¹¥µ…°ü9¼°¹…ÑÕÉ”­¹½İÌ¹½Ñ¡¥¹œ½˜Ñ¡…ĞÍÑ…Ñ”½˜Í…‘¹•ÍÌ¹q¹q¹!Õµ…¸‰•¥¹Ì…±½¹”¡…Ù”±½ÍĞÑ¡•¥Èİ…ä°Ñ¡¥¹­¥¹œÑ¡•µÍ•±Ù•ÌÍ¼İ¥Í”…¹±•Ù•È¸e½ÕÈ¥¹Ñ•±±•Ğ¥Ìå½ÕÈ¥±±¹•ÍÌ¸¼¹½Ğ‰”Ñ½¼±•Ù•È¸-¹½Üİ¡•¸Ñ¼ÍÑ½À°‰•™½É”å½ÔÑ…­”Ñ¡¥¹ÌÑ½¼™…È¹q¹q¹=¹”µ•…ÍÕÉ”½˜İ¥Í