  "53": {
    "name": "Fighting",
    "main_text": "It was here a moment ago. Now it is gone. For a little while we inhabit the present moment. A moment later we leave it.\n\nAnd in that brief interval, how much violence, emotion, fighting, conflict, anger and hatred! All for this one moment!\n\nWe are like people waiting for a train on the platform. Unable to sit still, we turn on one another, hurt one another, try to dominate and possess one another. **Politics in full fury.**\n\nThen suddenly the train arrives and we disappear for good.",
    "commentary": "A fighting temper or a simmering rage often conceals deep pain. We think that if we hurt others we will be spared hurt ourselves.\n\nIn fact, the opposite happens. A wound covered in armour cannot heal. And if we use it as a weapon against someone else, we shut out the love and nourishment we need in order to heal.\n\nIf you recognise yourself in this, it is time to lay down your arms. There is so much love to receive if you will allow it. **Begin by forgiving yourself. You are worth it.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "54": {
    "name": "Mind",
    "main_text": "This is how I see your head. Steering wheels, pedals, all sorts of odds and ends you have picked up here and there and piled up any old way. **A proper junk heap.**\n\nYour skull is crammed with things that crowd out your living space. They never stop rattling and creaking in your head. It keeps you occupied.\n\nTake the time to look closely at your thoughts. One day, sit down quietly on your own. For half an hour, write down everything that comes into your mind. Then you will see what I mean.\n\nYou will be surprised at what goes on in your head. The chaos there is everywhere. It wraps you in a fog of thoughts through which you can neither see reality nor find spiritual clarity.\n\nYou need to let the mist clear. The simple resolve to do so is enough for it to lift of its own accord. **Remember, the fog is not clinging to you. You are the one who won't let it go!**",
    "commentary": "The Page of Clouds tells you that somebody is thoroughly stuck in their head. Watch out, **it might be you!**\n\n----------"
  },
  "55": {
    "name": "Consciousness",
    "main_text": "We come from the unknown and we return to it. We keep coming back. We have been here thousands of times and we will be here again.\n\nYou are an immortal being inhabiting a body. The body is a physical form, and it is fleeting. The things we live within, our home, our body, our intellect, all arise from matter. With time they wear out and die.\n\nYet your conscious intelligence, which the Buddha and Bodhidharma call no-mind, transcends matter and goes beyond body and mind. **It lies beyond the physical world.**\n\nNo-mind is eternal. It takes form and returns to the source of the unknown. This passage between the known and the unknown repeats itself over and over until our consciousness is enlightened.\n\nA fully realised being is living their last incarnation. Once the flower has opened, it does not come back. Having found its deepest nature, it has nothing more to learn in the school of life.\n\nWhoever understands that life is a schooling in the cycle of life and death is free of all the veils of illusion. **They will pass from the known into the unknowable, beyond even the unknown.**",
    "commentary": "When this card appears in a reading, it means that a crystal clarity is now yours. You are experiencing a detachment rooted in the deepest silence at the heart of your being.\n\nYou no longer wish to grasp things with your intellect. Your understanding has become universal, in tune with the pulse of life.\n\nAccept this wonderful gift and **share it with others.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "56": {
    "name": "Schizophrenia",
    "main_text": "At this moment, you are not who you truly are. You have no existence of your own because you have no centre. You are like a crowd, a public square ringing with a multitude of different voices.\n\nThe instant you say â€œyes,â€ a â€œnoâ€ comes running. You cannot say â€œyesâ€ with your whole heart. **This leaves no room for happiness.**\n\nWhen you come apart inside, pain and suffering always follow.",
    "commentary": "The figure on this card is a modern picture of Buridan's donkey, who died because he could not choose between a bucket of water and a bale of hay. That is exactly where we find ourselves when we are caught in indecision, with the mind pulling us two ways.\n\nShould I go forward or back? This way or that? Say yes or say no? Whatever we eventually decide, in this frame of mind we will always think we might have chosen better.\n\nThe only way out of the dilemma is to choose neither and let go of both at once. Listing the pros and cons or thinking the problem to death will not give you an answer.\n\nIt is wiser to trust your heart and follow it. First, then, find your heart. If you can't, just jump. **Your heart will beat so fast you'll have no trouble finding it!**\n\n----------"
  },
  "57": {
    "name": "Ice-olation",
    "main_text": "You can live within existence or make your ego your centre. You cannot do both at the same time.\n\nWhen you focus your energy on your ego, you cut yourself off from existence. You live on an island hemmed in by boundaries you have drawn yourself. For you there is only â€œmeâ€ and â€œnot me.â€\n\nThat split is the ego, a state of isolation that hardens you. Your energy ceases to flow and gets stuck. People become like ice cubes, utterly without warmth. They have no love.\n\nThe warmth of love can melt them, and the boundaries disappear. In love, as in joy, there is no separation. **Neither love nor joy has any coldness in it.**",
    "commentary": "The many-coloured tears of the figure on this card show the way out of â€œice-olation.â€ Tears, and tears alone, can melt the ice that has formed inside us.\n\nThere is healing in crying, and nothing to be ashamed of. Crying helps us let go of our pain. We grow softer and gentler with ourselves, and **our tears help us heal.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "58": {
    "name": "Postponement",
    "main_text": "It is foolish to put off a decision you could make today. Tomorrow you will still have to decide. So why not decide today?\n\nDo you honestly think your mind will be clearer tomorrow? That you will be cleverer, younger and more vigorous than you are today? Tomorrow you will be older, less courageous, richer in experience but one step closer to death. You will tremble more and your fear will be greater.\n\nNever put things off until tomorrow. There is no certainty that tomorrow will ever become today. **If you have a decision to make, make it now.**",
    "commentary": "â€œNever put off till tomorrow what you can do todayâ€ is a saying few people take to heart. Yet when we put things off, they weigh on us.\n\nLet go of your doubts and you will feel relieved. **You'll wonder why you waited so long.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "59": {
    "name": "Comparison",
    "main_text": "Comparison keeps feelings of inferiority and superiority alive. When you stop comparing, those feelings fall away and you simply are.\n\nIt doesn't matter whether you are a scrubby bush or a towering tree. You are yourself. And existence wants you exactly as you are.\n\nA blade of grass is as necessary as the greatest star. Without that blade of grass, something would be missing from the divine.\n\nThe cuckoo's call has the same worth as the Buddha's words. Without the cuckoo, the world would be poorer.\n\nLook around you. Everything is needed, and everything has its place in existence. It forms a living whole in which nothing is higher and nothing lower. **No being is inferior or superior to another. Each is unique, beyond comparison.**",
    "commentary": "Face the truth. There will always be someone more beautiful, more gifted, stronger, cleverer and happier than you.\n\nThere will also always be someone less fortunate. Comparing yourself with others will not tell you who you really are.\n\nLook within yourself instead and see whether you are putting your own potential to use.\n\n----------"
  },
  "60": {
    "name": "The Burden",
    "main_text": "Truth is nothing you have to attain. It is always here. Our work is simply to clear away the lies.\n\nEvery goal, every ideal, every ideology, religion and doctrine is deceptive by nature. Take care not to fall under their influence.\n\nRecognise how readily the person you are today lends itself to falsehood. How easy it is for others to manipulate you and make you into whatever they want.\n\nLooking for truth keeps you busy. You skirt what matters without ever touching it. This is how a lie stays hidden. Become aware of it and learn to tell falsehood from truth deep within yourself.\n\nOnce you acknowledge what is false in your personality, it disappears. When you stop seeking truth, you will no longer live a lie, because you will no longer need to. **When the lie goes, truth remains.**",
    "commentary": "If life feels to you like one long struggle from birth to death, it is time to free your shoulders and carry on walking with nobody on your back.\n\nFeel how light you are now. You have mountains of your own to climb. Dreams of your own to realise.\n\nYou need your energy to fulfil your wishes. You will always be short of it until you let go of the expectations you have taken on from others.\n\n----------"
  },
  "61": {
    "name": "Politics",
    "main_text": "Anyone false and hypocritical is a potential political or religious leader. All it takes is a knack for deceiving people, a little cunning and a mask you can hide behind.\n\nPoliticians and priests lead a double life. They live behind a faÃ§ade. The faÃ§ade deceives. The truth is behind it.\n\nA face whose expressions look innocent has in fact been carefully studied and rehearsed. If you want to know the truth, look at what that face conceals.\n\nThere you will see the politician, the priest, stripped bare. **These two kinds of cunning people have ruled humanity.**",
    "commentary": "Do you recognise this man? Even the most innocent and sincere among us have a politician who has taken over the mind.\n\nThe mind acts like a politician hungry for power. It devises plans and tactics to manipulate situations and people for the sole purpose of getting what it wants.\n\nLook closely at yourself. Have you played this shabby game too? What you learn about yourself may hurt, but it will hurt more to keep playing a game that does nobody any good, least of all you.\n\n**Whatever you gain this way will slip like sand through your fingers.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "62": {
    "name": "Guilt",
    "main_text": "Forget everything you know about sin and virtue. Both are foolish, and between them they have robbed humanity of the joy of living.\n\nThe sinner feels guilty, and guilt destroys their joy. How can you feel happy if you spend your time reproaching yourself and going to church to confess, always seeking forgiveness for what you have done, always trying to unburden your heart?\n\nUnder those conditions it is impossible to take delight in life. You feel heavy and weighed down. Remorse is like great stones crushing your chest, and with all that weight you cannot dance.\n\nWhat place does remorse have in dancing, in music, in love, in life? Someone who feels guilty is not living. They are depressed. **They live as if they were dead, the light gone out of their heart.**",
    "commentary": "You are fine just as you are. It is perfectly natural to make mistakes sometimes.\n\nLearn from your mistakes, carry on your way and **take care not to fall into the same trap again.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "63": {
    "name": "Sorrow",
    "main_text": "Pain is one way of becoming aware. It is only when the arrow pierces your heart and wounds you deeply that your awareness wakes up.\n\nWhen life is easy, comfortable and pleasant, nothing troubles you. But when a friend dies, an opportunity opens up.\n\nWhen the woman you love leaves you, your life seems to sink into darkness and you ache with loneliness. You loved her so much, and then one day it is all over and she goes.\n\nThe pain and the tears that follow are a blessed opportunity for you to become aware. The arrow hurts terribly, yet it also has its use.\n\n**The nature of pain is to awaken your awareness, rather than to make you miserable.** When your innermost being wakes up, your suffering ceases.",
    "commentary": "Great suffering has an enormous power to transform. For a change to take place, though, we have to go deep within ourselves, all the way down to the roots of our pain.\n\nSurrender to the pain. Accept it as it is, without looking for someone to blame and without self-pity.\n\n----------"
  },
  "64": {
    "name": "Rebirth",
    "main_text": "Zen says that you come from nowhere and go nowhere. You are simply here, in the present moment, neither leaving nor arriving anywhere.\n\nEverything flows through you. Your deepest awareness lets the world outside pass through without identifying with it. It simply reflects what passes.\n\nWhen a lion roars in front of a mirror, do you think the mirror roars back? When the lion leaves and a happy child stands before the mirror in its place, does the mirror start laughing with the child?\n\nNo, the mirror does nothing. It simply reflects what is. Your awareness is like that mirror. You neither come nor go. It is the events outside you that come and go.\n\nYou are born, you grow old and you die. **These are only reflections on the eternal lake of consciousness.**",
    "commentary": "Whatever your state of awareness at the moment, whether you feel listless, depressed, angry or rebellious, know that you can grow and reach a new level of awareness if you are willing.\n\nYou are going through **a time of growth and change.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "65": {
    "name": "Abundance",
    "main_text": "In the East, the body and matter have been condemned. Material things are called â€œillusoryâ€ (maya), things that seem to exist but have no real substance. Matter is said to be made of the same stuff as dreams.\n\nThe East, having denied the world, finds itself poor, sick and in misery. One half of humanity has embraced the inner world and rejected the outer. The other half has favoured the material world and ignored inner knowledge.\n\nThese two attitudes each fall short of a whole. **A person who is missing the other half of their being can never feel happy.**\n\nWe need to be whole, integrated, rich in the life of the body, in science, in meditation and in conscious intelligence. To my mind only a whole person is both healthy and holy.\n\nI want Zorba and the Buddha to become one. By himself, Zorba is empty. His dance has no lasting meaning. It is the joy of a moment. Sooner or later he will tire of dancing.\n\nTo know fullness you must drink from the inexhaustible springs the cosmos offers you. To be whole, you must take root in existence itself.",
    "commentary": "The King of Rainbows stands for a time of inner integration, of feminine and masculine energies, of earth and sky.\n\nSay â€œyes.â€ Become whole, with all the colours of the rainbow shining through you. **You will see that existence supports you in all you do.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "66": {
    "name": "Flowering",
    "main_text": "Zen urges you to live fully, totally, intensely. Christianity would have you turn the flame down low. Zen would have you live with all the energy overflowing in you.\n\nLet your vitality spread and nourish others. Bliss, blessing and ecstasy need not stay locked inside you like a seed of possibility. Let that seed open like a flower and send its fragrance out to everyone around it, to strangers as well as friends.\n\nThis is true compassion, true love. **You share your inner light, your celebration of the unseen.**\n\nThe Queen of Rainbows is sensual, alive and brimming with possibility. She snaps her fingers to the melody of love. On her zodiac necklace, the sign of Venus rests over her heart.\n\nFlowers rain down on her in harmony with her own flowering, and the waters of emotion swirl joyfully beneath the blossom that bears her.",
    "commentary": "Perhaps you feel like a garden in bloom just now, receiving blessings from every direction.\n\nWelcome the bees. Invite the birds to drink your nectar. **Let your joy radiate so that everyone can share it.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "67": {
    "name": "Slowing Down",
    "main_text": "Meditation is a kind of medicine. Its use is temporary. Once you understand what it means simply to be in a meditative state, you will no longer need any particular method of meditation.\n\nMeditation will be everywhere in your life. Walking is Zen. Sitting is Zen. How, then, will this find its own expression in you?\n\nYour life is guided by alertness, conscious intelligence, unconditional joy and affection, with a clear channel through which energy flows.\n\nYour walk will become a stroll. You will sit with love, alert and attentive, with no aim and no particular reason. Simply because it is lovely to sit doing nothing, to relax and rest!\n\nIn the same way, after a long walk you will sit down beneath a tree and enjoy the breeze as it cools you.\n\nEach moment of life can be a chance to feel the purity within, without trying to improve, cultivate or practise anything.\n\nWalking is Zen and sitting is Zen, speaking or keeping silent, moving or staying still. **The essence is at ease. The essence is at ease.** That is the key.\n\nDo whatever you wish. Deep within, you remain serene, relaxed, calm and centred.",
    "commentary": "There is nothing you need to do. Simply rest in your serenity.\n\nEnjoy slowing down, enjoy the stillness, and **realise that you are already at home.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "68": {
    "name": "Adventure",
    "main_text": "Truth, says Zen, has nothing to do with authority, tradition or the past. It is a radical, personal knowing, an individual experience. Each of us must discover it for ourselves.\n\nThere is security in the knowledge we start with. Searching for your own truth is a deeply uncertain undertaking. No one can guarantee you anything.\n\nIf you ask me for guarantees, I will tell you that only the dangers are certain. I can promise you that at any moment you may lose your way, and that your chances of reaching the goal are very small.\n\nYet one thing is sure. **The very act of searching for your own truth helps you grow.** I can promise you inner growth.\n\nYou will have to face dangers and make sacrifices, setting out each day into unknown, unpredictable country, without a map or a guide.\n\nYes, it will be hard going and you will often lose your way. But it is the only way to mature. We grow by passing through uncertainty.\n\nOnly someone who meets the challenge of the uncertain comes to know their inner truth.",
    "commentary": "Whenever we approach something new and unknown with the trust of a child, innocent, open and vulnerable, **the smallest things in life can become the greatest adventures.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "69": {
    "name": "Maturity",
    "main_text": "The difference between a seed and a flower in bloom is the same as the difference between the moment when you do not know you are a buddha and the moment you discover that you are.\n\nIn truth, you can be nothing other than a radiant inner light. **The buddha within is a being in full bloom, entirely open.** Every petal of its lotus has unfolded.",
    "commentary": "The figure on this card can move in any direction, inward or outward, because his joy and maturity are independent of what happens around him.\n\nHe is centred in his heart, and he is expanding. The brilliant white light protects and guides him. All his experiences in life have brought him to this point of perfection.\n\nThis card is a reward for someone who has worked hard. The effort is now bearing fruit. You stand on firm ground, and success and fulfilment crown your work.\n\n**This is the fruit of what you have already accomplished within yourself.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "70": {
    "name": "Moment to Moment",
    "main_text": "The past is over and the future has yet to appear. Neither has any actual form. The past has lost its form, and the future has yet to acquire one.\n\nTo live in the space between them is to live from moment to moment, your arrow trained on the one moment that has real form, the present.\n\nWhen awareness rests in the here and now, your whole being is absorbed in the reality of this moment. **This is the only path to the golden gate.**\n\nThe present is the golden gate. The here and now is the golden gate.",
    "commentary": "This card invites us to bring our attention back from what is elsewhere and different, and give it to what is happening here and now.\n\nAccept the way things unfold. Don't worry if you stumble. Pick yourself up, dust off your clothes and carry on your way.\n\n----------"
  },
  "71": {
    "name": "Guidance",
    "main_text": "You look outside yourself for a guide because you have yet to recognise the guide within you.\n\nYour task is to find that guide, that witness within, the Dharma, your inner buddha. When you awaken your own buddha, your life will be filled with grace and blessings.\n\nFor now, you cannot imagine the depth of goodness and divinity that awaits you. If your inner world is dark, find your way to the light within.\n\nOne small candle is enough to light up the darkness. Once you find your inner light you will know the way out of the dark and into a higher awareness.\n\nWhat follows is entirely natural. You do not stop to think or grope about or bump into walls, because you know instinctively where the way out is. **You know where to go, without hesitating or having to think it through.**",
    "commentary": "Your inner light is trying to show you the way. Your inner guide speaks only in a whisper, and you aren't sure you have understood. That is why you hesitate.\n\nYet the message of this card is clear. Listen closely to the voice of your inner guide and it will lead you to your centre. You will act from there, whole and true to yourself, because your energy will no longer be directed outward.\n\n**If you let it, the light will lead you exactly where you need to go.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "72": {
    "name": "The Miser",
    "main_text": "In clinging to what you have, you deprive yourself of something fundamental to life, the chance to expand and to share.\n\nThe moment you cling to things, you lose your centre. Material possessions cannot bring you to your essential goal. The purpose of your life is you, your own being.\n\nWhat matters is to have a beautiful soul. A beautiful house cannot give you that. In the same way, a fortune is no substitute for inner riches.\n\nWhat counts, beyond everything you can accumulate, is **an open heart, aware and receptive to all that exists.**",
    "commentary": "This card invites us to look at the things we are attached to. They have become so precious to us that we have built a fortress around them for protection.\n\nIt needn't be a handsome bank balance or a box full of jewels. It might be as simple as withholding time from a friend, or being afraid to tell someone you love them for fear of rejection.\n\nIf we block a spring, the water grows cloudy, stagnates and becomes undrinkable. If we lock up our riches and are unwilling to share them with others, they too lose their value and become useless.\n\nRemember that material things may one day be taken from you. **Open your heart and enjoy the freedom that sharing brings.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "73": {
    "name": "The Outsider",
    "main_text": "You feel left out. That's all right. You have just entered a time of transition. Take care now not to let pain and despair overwhelm you.\n\nYou think God has abandoned you and that nobody is left to comfort you. What you have yet to discover is that you need no comforting!\n\nHumanity has come of age. Be a grown man or woman and stand on your own two feet. The only way to connect with existence is to look inside yourself.\n\nThe centre of your being has always been connected to life. At birth you were separated from your mother. That separation was necessary for you to become a person in your own right and live a life of your own.\n\nBut you were never cut off from the universe. An invisible tie connects you to it, a tie grounded in awareness.\n\nTo feel your connection with the universe, you must reach this level of awareness by looking deeply within, clear-eyed and attentive. Then you will find the path that connects you to your conscious heart.\n\n**The buddha deep in your heart is the link.**",
    "commentary": "When we are left out or turned away, it is the little child in us who feels abandoned and alone. That is hardly surprising, since the feeling has its roots in experiences from our earliest childhood.\n\nYou now have a chance to discover where that feeling began, to recognise the pain and to pass through it until you are free.\n\nAs things become clear within you, you will see that the gate is unlocked. **You can reach what you long for most.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "74": {
    "name": "Compromise",
    "main_text": "Try to understand why you make compromises. Sooner or later you will see how little good this does you.\n\nIt is a way of avoiding a real decision or pushing down your confusion. Never push anything down. See your situation clearly.\n\nIf things are muddled, accept that. Know that you are confused. You will have taken your first step towards clarity. **Then the journey can begin.**",
    "commentary": "The two figures on this card bring to mind the petty, dishonest situations we can get ourselves into when we compromise our own truth.\n\nIt is one thing to show understanding towards others, to accept a point of view that differs from our own and to try to bring opposing forces together. It is another to submit at the cost of betraying who we are.\n\nWhen we look closely at our behaviour, we often find that we are trying to gain something, perhaps power or someone else's approval.\n\nWhen that prospect tempts you, take care. **In the end, all that kind of compromise leaves you with is a bitter aftertaste.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "75": {
    "name": "Patience",
    "main_text": "We have forgotten what patience is. Yet nothing is more precious than the ability to wait for the right moment.\n\nAll of existence knows how to be patient. A tree knows when to flower and when to let its leaves fall and stand bare under the sky. Even stripped of its leaves, the tree is beautiful.\n\nIt waits for spring with confidence. Knowing it will blossom again, it waits for the season of renewal without haste or impatience.\n\nHuman beings have lost that ability. We want everything to happen quickly. Our lack of patience is a loss for humanity.\n\nWhen you wait in silence, something grows within you. **Your essential, authentic self unfolds.**",
    "commentary": "The woman on this card is patient. Deep down she knows that all she can do is wait and let nature take its course.\n\nShe is neither drowsy nor indifferent. She knows the time has come to prepare for something wonderful. It is a lovely time, like the hour just before daybreak, when **waiting is exactly the right thing to do.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "76": {
    "name": "Ordinariness",
    "main_text": "There are moments when you feel centred and whole. They are rare. You look out at the ocean in all its wild vastness and suddenly forget your divided self, the feeling of coming apart inside. You relax.\n\nOr you are walking in the mountains and see pure snow, and for a second you feel as if you were in the Himalayas. A freshness of being comes over you. You feel quite simply yourself, with no need to put on an act. There is nobody there to play along.\n\nYou have come back inside yourself, back to your centre. It can happen when you listen to music, too. In such moments you feel a peace and happiness within, and a sense of grace and wholeness settles over you. You feel fulfilled, awake, complete.\n\nThere is no need to wait for these moments. They are there in everyday life. The philosophy of Zen is precisely to live the ordinary in an extraordinary way.\n\nThe most ordinary task, chopping wood or carrying water, can become an act of complete harmony. You can be happy cleaning the floor, cooking or doing the washing. It all depends on the spirit in which you do it.\n\n**All it takes is to be fully present and bring joy to what you are doing.**",
    "commentary": "Meet whatever situation arises with calm and simplicity, just as you are. You will do far better than if you try to be perfect, clever and extraordinary.\n\nLet go of the need to come out on top or to keep impressing your friends with your exploits.\n\nThe best gift you can give right now is to **hold life lightly, go one step at a time and take it as it comes.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "77": {
    "name": "Ripeness",
    "main_text": "Only when meditation has helped you find the light that shines through all your nights will you feel that death is a door opening onto the divine.\n\nWhen light enfolds your heart, death becomes a passage into universal spirit, where you become one with the ocean of existence.\n\nUntil you have known this ocean, you will have lived in vain. The present is here and now, and the fruit is always ripe.\n\nThe present moment is always the right one. It is up to you to find the courage to enter your inner forest. **The ripe fruit waits only for you before it drops. The moment is always right, never too early and never too late.**",
    "commentary": "This card tells you that you are ready to share your inner riches, the sap of your life. Simply relax wherever you are and accept what is.\n\nYour creativity can find expression in many ways, in your work, in your relationships and in the things you do every day.\n\nYou have no preparations to make and no special effort is called for. **The time has simply come.**\n\n----------"
  },
  "78": {
    "name": "We Are the World",
    "main_text": "When thousands upon thousands of people all around the earth celebrate their ecstasy, singing and dancing in their divine intoxication, collective suicide becomes absolutely impossible.\n\nCan you imagine war arising in that atmosphere of celebration and joy, of natural, spontaneous vitality and health? No.\n\nLife was given to you so that you could create, so that you could live in joy and happiness. When you weep, you are alone. When you celebrate, all existence joins in.\n\n**Celebration alone opens us to the ultimate, to the eternal.** Only unconditional joy allows us to move beyond the cycle of death and life.",
    "commentary": "When we discover the common source of our humanity, the place from which our dreams, our desires, our hopes and our fears all spring, we recognise that we are united in the great miracle of existence.\n\nWhen we bring our immense inner riches together to make a circle of love and wisdom that is open to everyone, **we help draw the wondrous outline of an everlasting creation.**\n\n----------"
  }
}
